  "claim_short": "Candidate new full counterexample for Problems 6.1 and 6.2 of arXiv:2202.06343. Omega=[0,2) union [3,4) is a level-three multi-tile but not a tile by Z, while G(chi_Omega,Z x Z) is a Riesz basis of L2(R). On the Zak square the multiplier is 1+z+z^3, with exact squared bounds (47-14 sqrt(7))/27 and 9. A general finite-mask criterion is proved. The example also contradicts source Theorems 1.3 and 1.4 as stated; their...",
